    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.operators\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI'm trying to keymap `S` to _replace until end of line_ just like `Y` does for _yanking_, but I cannot get it to work\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nv0.10.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"S\", require(\"mini.operators\").replace()..\"$\", { expr = true, replace_keycodes = false })\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nGiven\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/71b5694a2df4f7e3661855eb8e2814980d2e0ac9/lua/mini/operators.lua#L460-L468\r\nand\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/71b5694a2df4f7e3661855eb8e2814980d2e0ac9/lua/mini/operators.lua#L548\r\nI should be able to make an expression mapping for _replace until eol_  with the above code\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`E15: Invalid expression: \"<80><fd>hechon \"\"^Mg@$\"`",
